- Inspector of one class of the document: every port it has, own and inherited,
- with an editor for the value of each. Every edit lands in the AST and is written
- straight back as source text.
-
- The class is handed in as source. Which class that is — which node is picked on
- the canvas — is somebody else's question.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md sections 1 and 5
$bog_vmap_app_inspect $mol_view
	- Source of the class. The truth; everything below is derived from it.
	source? \
	- Other classes of the same document, so that a node typed with one of them
	- resolves its ports like any other. Empty is the honest default: an inspector
	- handed a lone class has no siblings, and inventing some would be worse than
	- having none.
	peers /$mol_tree2
	- Deployed MAM module the inherited ports are read from.
	pack? \https://mol.hyoo.ru
	sub /
		<= Head $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Title $mol_view sub / <= class_title \
				<= Base $mol_view sub / <= base_title \
				<= Total $mol_view sub / <= total \
		- Layout of the node, above the ports: on a page these five decide what the
		- thing looks like, and hunting them down among two dozen inherited ports is
		- not what an inspector is for. They are keys of `style` all the same.
		<= Flex $bog_vmap_app_inspect_flex
			value*? <=> flex_value*? \
		<= Body $mol_scroll
			sub /
				<= Rows $mol_view sub <= rows /
	- The document model. `source` is bound both ways, so a write through any
	- property below serializes the whole class and comes back out here as text.
	Node $bog_vmap_lang_node
		source? <=> source?
	- Where inherited ports come from. The class of the document is handed to the
	- library as well, so that `props_map` resolves the chain through it and
	- `props_owner` can tell an own port from an inherited one.
	Lib $bog_vmap_lib
		pack <= pack
		classes <= classes /
	Row* $bog_vmap_app_inspect_row
		sign <= row_sign* \
		owner <= row_owner* \
		inherited <= row_inherited* false
		value? <=> row_value*? $mol_tree2_empty
		keyed? <=> row_keyed*? false
		changeable? <=> row_changeable*? false
		drop? <=> row_drop*? null
		binds <= binds /string
		nodes <= nodes *

- Stand for the inspector: the source of the whole DOCUMENT on the left, the
- inspector of one of its classes on the right, so that an edit and the line it
- moves are on screen at once — and so that the lines it must NOT move are on
- screen too.
-
- A document and not a class, because that is where the editing of one class is
- dangerous: the class model writes what it touched as the whole text, and a stand
- of one class could never show the neighbour it eats.
-
- Which class is inspected is picked here by hand. Picking a node on the canvas is
- task 2.5, and until it exists a stand that pretends to have it would be testing
- nothing.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_demo $mol_view
	source? \
	sub /
		<= Source $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Source_head $mol_view
					sub /
						<= Source_title $mol_view sub / \Исходник документа
						<= Class_pick $mol_select
							hint \класс
							value? <=> klass? \
							options <= names /string
				<= Source_text $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_area
					rows 26
					value? <=> source?
		<= Inspect $bog_vmap_app_inspect
			source? <=> class_source? \
			peers <= trees /$mol_tree2
	- The document. One text, several classes, and a write through one of them
	- leaves the others alone.
	Doc $bog_vmap_lang_doc
		source? <=> source?
